response:
The threat incident involves the distribution of a malicious PowerPoint presentation ("Доповідь_050722_4.ppt") referencing the Ukrainian Operational Command "South" to target Ukrainian state organizations. The macro in the presentation creates a shortcut file ("gksg023ig.lnk") and an executable ("sgegkseg23mjl.exe"). The shortcut is executed via rundll32.exe to launch the executable, which is obfuscated with ConfuserEx. This executable downloads an image file ("thumb_d_F3D14F4982A256B5CDAE9BD579429AE7.jpg") from onyangdol[.]site, extracts and executes an intermediate .NET payload ("MCMDiction.exe"), which ultimately decrypts and executes the AgentTesla info-stealer malware.

